<title>UK: AllgemeineHypo plans to increase July99 Pfandbrief.</title>
<headline>AllgemeineHypo plans to increase July99 Pfandbrief.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allgemeine Hypothekenbank said on Monday it planned to add 1.0 billion marks to its 3.25 percent July 1999 Pfandbrief.  </p>
<p>&quot;Subject to market conditions the add-on will be launched tomorrow morning (June 3) at a spread flat to the 6.375 percent Treuhand obligation due July 7, 1999,&quot; the bank said.</p>
<p>Allgemeine Hypothekenbank Oeffentliche Pfandbriefe are rated Aa2 by Moody's Investors Service.</p>
<p>Joint lead managers for the transaction are ABN AMRO Hoare Govett, Commerzbank, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, DG Bank and Dresdner KB.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
